- Real DOM APIs, `createElement`/`textContent`/`setAttribute` — no `innerHTML` with interpolated content (this module mostly reads/toggles attributes rather than creating new elements, so this constraint is easy to satisfy).
- Strict TS, no `any`.
- Scope all queries to the `container` parameter, not `document`, so this composes correctly inside `main.ts` alongside the other `mount*` functions.

